parameters.text:
=You are an intake lead. A colleague has submitted a work request. Decide whether it can be scoped, how big it is, and exactly which questions are still missing.

Request type: {{ $json["Request type"] }}
What they need: {{ $json["What do you need"] }}
Who it is for: {{ $json["Who is it for"] }}
When: {{ $json["When do you need it"] }}

Set verdict to "not_actionable" only if this is a support or bug report rather than a piece of work, or if it is so vague that no reasonable question would rescue it. Otherwise "actionable".

Set complexity to "quick" if you could scope this today with what you already have, "standard" if a handful of answers would settle it, "complex" if there are real unknowns about systems, data, stakeholders or compliance.

For questions, list ONLY what you genuinely cannot infer. Never ask something they already answered above, and never ask for information you could reasonably assume. Each question needs a plain-English label written as a question, a type from text, textarea, number, date or dropdown, a short why, and for dropdown a list of concrete options. Return an empty questions array when complexity is quick.

parameters.jsCode:
const a = $json.output || {};
const t = $('Receive the Request').first().json;
return [{ json: {
  complexity: a.complexity || 'quick',
  restated: a.restated_need || '',
  answersText: '(No follow-up questions were needed - the request was already clear enough to scope.)',
  requester: t['Requester email'] || ''
} }];

parameters.text:
=Write a scoping brief a delivery team could pick up on Monday.

Original request ({{ $("Receive the Request").first().json["Request type"] }}): {{ $("Receive the Request").first().json["What do you need"] }}
Who it is for: {{ $("Receive the Request").first().json["Who is it for"] }}
Timing: {{ $("Receive the Request").first().json["When do you need it"] }}
How we read it: {{ $json.restated }}
Complexity: {{ $json.complexity }}

Follow-up answers:
{{ $json.answersText }}

Be concrete and short. Out of scope matters as much as in scope - name the things a requester usually assumes are included but are not. Assumptions must be things you inferred rather than things you were told, so that the requester can correct them on the next screen. Effort band should be one of: Small (under a week), Medium (one to three weeks), Large (over a month), Needs a spike first. If something is still genuinely unknown, put it in open_questions rather than inventing an answer.

parameters.jsCode:
const a = $json.output || {};
const cap = a.complexity === 'complex' ? 8 : 4;
const allowed = ['text', 'textarea', 'number', 'date', 'dropdown'];
const asked = Array.isArray(a.questions) ? a.questions.slice(0, cap) : [];
const fields = asked.map(function (q) {
  const t = allowed.indexOf(q.type) === -1 ? 'text' : q.type;
  const f = { fieldLabel: String(q.label || 'Anything to add').slice(0, 120), fieldType: t, requiredField: false };
  if (t === 'dropdown') {
    const opts = (Array.isArray(q.options) ? q.options : []).filter(Boolean);
    f.fieldOptions = { values: (opts.length ? opts : ['Yes', 'No', 'Not sure']).map(function (o) { return { option: String(o).slice(0, 80) }; }) };
  } else if (t !== 'date' && t !== 'number') {
    f.placeholder = String(q.why || '').slice(0, 120);
  }
  return f;
});
fields.push({ fieldLabel: 'Anything else we should know', fieldType: 'textarea', requiredField: false, placeholder: 'Optional' });
return [{ json: { formJson: JSON.stringify(fields), questionCount: fields.length } }];

const a = $('Assess the Request').first().json.output || {};
const t = $('Receive the Request').first().json;
const skip = ['submittedAt', 'formMode', 'formQueryParameters'];
const ans = $json;
const lines = Object.keys(ans).filter(function (k) {
  return skip.indexOf(k) === -1 && ans[k] !== '' && ans[k] !== null && ans[k] !== undefined;
}).map(function (k) {
  const v = ans[k];
  return '- ' + k + ': ' + (typeof v === 'object' ? JSON.stringify(v) : v);
});
return [{ json: {
  complexity: a.complexity || 'standard',
  restated: a.restated_need || '',
  answersText: lines.length ? lines.join('\n') : '(No extra detail was given.)',
  requester: t['Requester email'] || ''
} }];

const b = $json.output || {};
const li = function (arr) {
  const a = Array.isArray(arr) && arr.length ? arr : ['Nothing noted'];
  return '<ul style="margin:4px 0 12px;padding-left:18px">' + a.map(function (x) { return '<li>' + String(x) + '</li>'; }).join('') + '</ul>';
};
const h = function (s) { return '<div style="font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7a8194;margin-top:14px">' + s + '</div>'; };
const preview = '<div style="text-align:left;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5">'
  + '<div style="font-weight:600;font-size:16px">' + (b.title || 'Untitled') + '</div>'
  + '<div style="color:#41485c;margin:4px 0 10px">' + (b.one_line || '') + '</div>'
  + h('Objective') + '<div>' + (b.objective || '') + '</div>'
  + h('In scope') + li(b.in_scope)
  + h('Out of scope') + li(b.out_of_scope)
  + h('We assumed') + li(b.assumptions)
  + h('Risks') + li(b.risks)
  + h('Effort band') + '<div>' + (b.effort_band || '') + '</div>'
  + h('Still open') + li(b.open_questions)
  + '</div>';
return [{ json: { previewHtml: preview, brief: b } }];

const b = $json.brief || {};
const revised = $json.revised === true;
const t = $('Receive the Request').first().json;
const li = function (arr) {
  const a = Array.isArray(arr) && arr.length ? arr : ['Nothing noted'];
  return '<ul style="margin:6px 0 18px;padding-left:20px">' + a.map(function (x) { return '<li style="margin:3px 0">' + String(x) + '</li>'; }).join('') + '</ul>';
};
const h = function (s) { return '<div style="font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7a8194;margin-top:22px">' + s + '</div>'; };
const row = function (k, v) { return '<tr><td style="padding:7px 0;color:#7a8194;width:170px;vertical-align:top">' + k + '</td><td style="padding:7px 0">' + (v || '-') + '</td></tr>'; };
const html = '<div style="font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,sans-serif;max-width:760px;margin:48px auto;padding:0 24px;color:#1f2430;line-height:1.55">'
  + '<div style="font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7a8194">Scoped brief' + (revised ? ' &middot; revised by the requester' : '') + '</div>'
  + '<h1 style="margin:8px 0 6px;font-size:28px;line-height:1.25">' + (b.title || 'Untitled request') + '</h1>'
  + '<p style="font-size:17px;color:#41485c;margin:0 0 8px">' + (b.one_line || '') + '</p>'
  + '<table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e8ee;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ee;margin:18px 0">'
  + row('Effort band', b.effort_band) + row('Suggested owner', b.suggested_team) + row('Requested by', t['Requester email']) + row('Needed by', t['When do you need it'])
  + '</table>'
  + h('Objective') + '<div>' + (b.objective || '') + '</div>'
  + h('In scope') + li(b.in_scope)
  + h('Out of scope') + li(b.out_of_scope)
  + h('Assumptions the requester confirmed') + li(b.assumptions)
  + h('Risks') + li(b.risks)
  + h('Dependencies') + li(b.dependencies)
  + h('Still open') + li(b.open_questions)
  + '<p style="margin-top:34px;font-size:13px;color:#7a8194;border-top:1px solid #e6e8ee;padding-top:14px">Nothing was filed automatically. Add a node after Render the Finished Brief to push this into your tracker, docs or chat tool.</p>'
  + '</div>';
return [{ json: { html: html, brief: b, revised: revised } }];

parameters.text:
=The requester read the brief below and corrected it. Rewrite the whole brief so it reflects what they said, and return the same structure.

Current brief:
{{ JSON.stringify($("Build the Preview").first().json.brief) }}

What the requester said should change:
{{ $json["What should change"] }}

Treat the requester as the authority on intent and scope, not on effort. If their correction makes the work bigger, move the effort band up and say so in risks rather than quietly absorbing it. Any assumption they contradicted must be removed, not softened. If their correction raises something you now cannot answer, add it to open_questions.
